codex
The compact calculation now reproduces the exact post-normalization degree pattern without the large raw \((\gamma,\pi)\)-system: after the constant spine, the four independent coefficient polynomials have degrees
\[
(2t-1,\ t-1,\ 2t,\ 2t).
\]
Their universal syzygies are already verified mechanically:
\(C_{03}=-C_{12}\), \(C_{02}=-b_1C_{12}-C_{11}\), and \(C_{10}=-yg\).
This proves the duplicate-row count once the three pivot families vanish, and it gives a much cheaper route to \(t=5,6\).
