+```text
+-19200 b3^2 b4^3+191000 b3 b4^6-406875 b4^9-1024,
+-b4^2(192 b3^2-8960 b3 b4^3+28925 b4^6),
+-b4^4(16 b3-35 b4^3),
+ b4^3(88 b3-295 b4^3).
+```
+
+The incompatible last two equations on `b4!=0`, followed by the first
+equation on `b4=0`, exhibit the terminal constant directly in this fiber.
+
+For `t=3`, the six expanded terminal rows are in
+`terminal_t3_canonical_side-first_exact.json`.  Dehomogenizing at `b4=1`,
+the three bands `3,4,5` alone have exact Gröbner basis `[1]` over `A_3`.
+This attractive three-row phenomenon does not persist as stated: in the
+banked `t=4` residual the last five and last six bands are nonunit modulo
